From: nvidia-generic <nvidia-generic@local>
Subject: [PATCH] ozone: nvidia-drm scanout CreateBuffer fallback

Test-modeset calls CreateBufferWithModifiers(SCANOUT, preferred mods).
On nvidia-drm the ChromeOS create+import verification loop often fails
even though plain CreateBuffer(SCANOUT|RENDERING) works — Ash then never
CommitModesets, SchedulePageFlip sees no controller_, and the AddFB shim
can only bootstrap a single SetCrtc (laggy UI, invisible cursor, tear).

Fall back to CreateBuffer without modifiers when the modifier path fails.

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/screen_manager.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/screen_manager.cc
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/screen_manager.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/screen_manager.cc
@@ -933,10 +933,26 @@
   // Get the buffer that best reflects what the next Page Flip will look like,
   // which is using the preferred modifiers from the controllers.
   std::unique_ptr<GbmBuffer> buffer =
       drm->gbm_device()->CreateBufferWithModifiers(
           fourcc_format, bounds.size(), GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT, modifiers);
+  if (!buffer) {
+    // nvidia-drm: modifier create+import verify fails; plain create works for
+    // compositor buffers (see gbm-minigbm-compat). Retry without modifiers.
+    LOG(WARNING) << "CreateBufferWithModifiers failed " << bounds.ToString()
+                 << " mods=" << modifiers.size()
+                 << "; retry CreateBuffer(SCANOUT|RENDERING)";
+    buffer = drm->gbm_device()->CreateBuffer(
+        fourcc_format, bounds.size(),
+        GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT | GBM_BO_USE_RENDERING);
+  }
   if (!buffer) {
     LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to create scanout buffer";
     return DrmOverlayPlaneList();
   }
